 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "594fa3b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Path2-Broad-category specialty classification using GloVeEmbeddings\n",
    "Applies the GloVe embedding branch to Path 2 (5 broad clinical superclasses, \n",
    "grouped from the original fine-grained specialties), to test whether reduced \n",
    "granularity improves classification robustness compared to Path 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline:**\n",
    "1. Loaded `super_clinical_mtsamples.csv`, using the pre-built `clinical_superclass` \n",
    "   column as the target label\n",
    "2. Tokenized transcription text using the same clinical stopword list as Path 1\n",
    "3. Built document vectors via mean-pooled GloVe embeddings (glove.6B.100d)\n",
    "4. Split into train/test, then tuned Linear SVC and Logistic Regression via \n",
    "   Grid Search (5-fold CV) on the training set only\n",
    "5. Evaluated the best model (Linear SVC, C=0.1) on the held-out test set\n",
    "\n",
    "**Results:**\n",
    "- Best model: Linear SVC (C=0.1)\n",
    "- Final test macro-F1: **0.572**\n",
    "- Strongest class: `surgical_and_procedural` (precision 0.81, recall 0.73, F1 0.77)\n",
    "- Weakest classes: `diagnostic_and_pathology` (F1 0.42) and `rehab_and_applied_health` \n",
    "  (F1 0.43) — both smallest classes (n=87, n=56), showing imbalance still limits \n",
    "  performance despite broader grouping\n",
    "\n",
    "**Comparison to Path 1:** Path 2's macro-F1 (0.572) exceeds Path 1's fine-grained \n",
    "result (0.515), supporting the hypothesis that broader categories are easier to \n",
    "classify — largely by resolving Surgery's vocabulary overlap problem (Path 1's \n",
    "weakest class, F1 0.51), which becomes `surgical_and_procedural`'s strongest \n",
    "result here (F1 0.77) once anatomically diverse surgical specialties are merged."
   ]
  },
